# M-15 execution inputs.
#
# The six addresses below are supplied by the wallet owner. Nothing here chooses or defaults one:
# an absent address is an error, never a guess, and the runners refuse to start without them.
#
# Copy the values you control into .env, which is git-ignored. Only public addresses belong here.
# Private keys are read from the environment at signing time and never appear in any artifact.

# --- already supplied from earlier missions ---
# MORDANT_ADDRESS_HOLDER_A=0x...
# MORDANT_ADDRESS_HOLDER_B=0x...

# --- the six still missing ---

# ROLE_BUYER. Creates the vault. Needs MON only: the live path stops before redemption,
# so the buyer never funds it.
MORDANT_ADDRESS_BUYER=

# ROLE_HOLDER, as the advancing party. Approves and advances at activation.
# Needs MON and 100000 atomic units of aUSDC.
# Must NOT be the buyer: the vault rejects a funder that is also the buyer.
MORDANT_ADDRESS_FUNDER=

# ROLE_ORIGINATOR. Signs two EIP-712 pledges and sends no transaction, but receives the net
# proceeds. Must not also be a facility or the buyer.
MORDANT_ADDRESS_ORIGINATOR=

# ROLE_FACILITY, the protected one. Calls activate.
MORDANT_ADDRESS_FACILITY_A=

# ROLE_FACILITY, the challenger. Commits and reveals the conflict.
# Must NOT equal FACILITY_A: a facility cannot raise a conflict against itself.
MORDANT_ADDRESS_FACILITY_B=

# No Mordant role. Holds MINTER_ROLE only between the grant and the revoke in phase D.
# Keep it disposable: it should not be a participant that outlives the ceremony.
MORDANT_ADDRESS_ISSUANCE_MINTER=

# --- notes on funding, which is what usually blocks a phase ---
#
# Every signer needs MON for gas. Six new addresses means six visits to the Monad faucet,
# which allows one claim per address per 24 hours, so start early.
#
# Only the funder needs aUSDC, and only the advance. The faucet's aUSDC treasury has been
# observed holding less than the advance, so plan the source before phase C1.
